2. Code derived from the Half-Life SDK and from Paranoia
--------------------------------------------------------

Much of src/ (the game DLLs, the shared code and the SDK headers) descends
from the Half-Life 1 SDK, Copyright (c) Valve Corp. That code is subject to
the Half-Life 1 SDK License, whose full text is in
LICENSES/Half-Life-1-SDK.txt: it may be copied, modified and distributed in
source and object code form, but only for free.

Code that descends from Paranoia (the client.dll renderer, and the Paranoia
and Spirit of Half-Life code in both game DLLs) keeps Paranoia's terms:
GPL-2.0 for Paranoia's own code and the Half-Life 1 SDK License for Valve's
files (see docs/refs.md).


3. Code and data reconstructed from the Cry of Fear binaries
------------------------------------------------------------

The rest of src/, and the names and addresses of retail functions and data
in tools/symbols/ and docs/*.csv, reproduce code and facts of the retail
Cry of Fear binaries. Their copyright belongs to their original authors:
Team Psykskallar (Cry of Fear), Valve Corporation (the GoldSrc engine, VGUI2
and the engine launcher) and the authors of the third-party code compiled
into the game. This license grants no rights over that code. It is
published for research, preservation and interoperability with a legally
owned copy of the game.


DeCoF is not affiliated with or endorsed by Team Psykskallar or Valve. No
game assets or retail binaries are part of this repository.
